refused: d207_spacing_and_checking.cy:7:24, line 7 column 24
 7 |     let $b: i32 set_to $a+1;
   |                        ^^^^
 fix:  `$a + 1`
 why:  a binary operator, `set_to` and word operators included, has one space on each side, so `1+8` is refused (D23, D213)

refused: d207_spacing_and_checking.cy:8:24, line 8 column 24
 8 |     let $c: i64 set_to $a;
   |                        ^^
 what: this is `i32`, where `i64` is needed
 why:  `:` doesn't convert, and `as` builds a new value of another type (D7)
